  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: This scene demonstrates the use of the Flyby behavior to create procedurally
    generated motion paths. Instead of creating paths with Bezier curves (as with
    Motion Path), Flyby creates a path from destination points, heading, and velocity.
    Each of the objects in this scene demonstrate different configurations of Flyby
    with many more possibilities available.
  Warning: 
  URLTitle: Flyby Documentation
  URL: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/automation/flyby
  URL2Title: 
  URL2: 
